# API Test Design Specification

## 1. Overview
Contract-driven API testing strategy for 15 microservices using Pact for consumer-driven contracts.

## 2. Service Coverage Matrix
| Service | Endpoints | Contract Tests | Integration Tests | Performance Tests |
|---------|-----------|----------------|-------------------|-------------------|
| User Service | 12 | 12 | 8 | 4 |
| Order Service | 15 | 15 | 10 | 6 |
| Payment Service | 8 | 8 | 6 | 4 |
| Inventory Service | 10 | 10 | 7 | 3 |
| Notification Service | 6 | 6 | 4 | 2 |

## 3. Authentication Flows
- JWT Bearer Token validation
- OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code flow
- API Key authentication for internal services
- mTLS for service-to-service communication

## 4. Test Data Strategy
- Synthetic test data generation per service
- Database seeding scripts for integration tests
- Contract test data isolated per provider/consumer pair
- PII-free datasets for all environments

## 5. Contract Testing Approach
- Consumer-driven contracts with Pact
- Provider verification in CI pipeline
- Contract publishing to Pact Broker
- Canary deployment with contract validation

## 6. Test Execution
- Unit/Contract tests: Every PR (2-3 min)
- Integration tests: Nightly (15 min)
- Performance tests: Weekly (30 min)
- Contract compatibility: On every deploy
